From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 18 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: Card.RegisterEffect keeps the zone opponent, an
 eliminated one gets no fallback at n > 2

Six official scripts (c40669071, c53244294, c73542331, c79569173, c92065772,
c97466438) pick zones with Duel.SelectDisableField in the target and register
the EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD effect with Card.RegisterEffect, whose operation
returns the label. Card.RegisterEffect did not record the opponent of the prompt,
so the high half of the value went to the next living opponent.

- fold::record_disfield_opp is used by Duel.RegisterEffect and Card.RegisterEffect.
  The opponent is the one of the last zone prompt of the running link (a slot in
  chain::zone_opp, found by the triggering effect, so another link cannot
  overwrite it), else the bound opponent. A recorded opponent that is
  eliminated later stays recorded.
- add_disabled_zones_n: a recorded opponent that is not alive gives an empty
  high half. The zones are not moved to another seat (F5: no fallback).
- f8_place_target: a bound opponent that is dead closes the high half, so
  SelectDisableField and SelectFieldZone give no prompt and no zone.
- Duel.SSet at n > 2 toward a dead bound opponent returns 0 and sets no card
  (it was set on the own field). n == 2 is unchanged.
---
